{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And this is the blessing</b> Above it is written: אשר אני נותן לבני ישראל (which I give to the children of Israel), and adjacent to it: וזאת הברכה. To say: I agree upon their blessing. וזאת הברכה — in gematria: זו היא התורה (this is the Torah). For by the merit of Torah, blessing." "<b>Moses man of Elohim</b> — ר\"ט (initial letters) מאה (one hundred). ס\"ת (final letters) משה. And this is: YHWH Elohim of your fathers add to you a thousand times (Deuteronomy 1:11). For they said to him: give him one hundred blessings every day, and each blessing ten gold pieces — behold one thousand. Therefore he said: YHWH add to you a thousand times, like משלי. And He shall bless you from His משל. The verse begins with vav and ends with vav, to say that he blessed twelve tribes."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:25:27.375070703Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}